issues.body:
## Description

Parent components have `keyPress` and `charTyped`  in their layout, however, these events are not triggered (I haven't checked the other events, they may have this bug as well). As a result, doing something like:

```java
var layout = UIContainers.verticalFlow(Sizing.content(), Sizing.content());
// other layout setup
layout.keyPress().subscribe(input -> {
    if (input.isUp()) {
        MyCode.doSomething();
        return true;
    } else if (input.input() == InputConstants.KEY_DELETE) {
        return MyCode.deleteSystem32();
    }
    return false;
});
```

requires the following workaround:

```java
@Override
public boolean onKeyPress(KeyEvent input) {
    return this.keyPressEvents.sink().onKeyPress(input) || super.onKeyPress(input);
}
```

Alternatively, the event has to be handled directly in `onKeyPress`

# Analysis

Both events contain something like:
https://github.com/wisp-forest/owo-lib/blob/1fb7971326ba945b5a2a9cf7985c451136dfdbbc/src/main/java/io/wispforest/owo/ui/base/BaseParentUIComponent.java#L258-L266

However, it would probably be better if they were implemented more like:

```java
@Override
public boolean onCharTyped(CharacterEvent input) {
    var focused = this.focusHandler == null ? null : this.focusHandler.focused();
    if (focused != null && focused.onCharTyped(input)) return true;

    return this.charTypedEvents.sink().onCharTyped(input) || super.onCharTyped(input);
}
```

This would make them behave more similarly to [`onMouseDown`](https://github.com/wisp-forest/owo-lib/blob/1fb7971326ba945b5a2a9cf7985c451136dfdbbc/src/main/java/io/wispforest/owo/ui/base/BaseParentUIComponent.java#L208-L214), which does work correctly

## Versions

fabric_api_version=0.158.0+26.2
owo_version=0.13.1+26.2

However, I'm fairly certain this has been happening for quite some time, I remember wondering why `keyEvent` and `charTyped` didn't work on many occasions

the minecraft function `private void componentHoverEffect(final Font font, final Style hoveredStyle, final int xMouse, final int yMouse)` has changed in the version `26.1` . previously the parameter was nullable but in the latest version they made it non nullable.

the LabelComponent however has this draw tooltip function with style function returning nulls
```java
@Override
public void drawTooltip(OwoUIGraphics context, int mouseX, int mouseY, float partialTicks, float delta) {
    super.drawTooltip(context, mouseX, mouseY, partialTicks, delta);
    context.componentHoverEffect(this.textRenderer, this.styleAt(mouseX - this.x, mouseY - this.y), mouseX, mouseY);
